{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-17d:000001:issue_created:sase-17d:16918e034623b05b91cb211136169fa08012f195283b00eb6f199ee1113f64ff","timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:16:45Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.0qd","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-17d","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-17d","title":"Agents tab agent data decks and cards","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-09-23T23:16:45Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.0qd","updated_at":"2026-09-23T23:16:45Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"The Agents tab replaces its metadata panel and its Files and LLM Calls panels with one deck-panel type. It shows one or two panels, stacked top and bottom or side by side, and each panel shows an agent data deck (Main, Files or Tools) made of agent data cards. A deck renders all of its cards on one page when they fit a configurable threshold and one card per page otherwise. Keys cycle cards (Ctrl+J/K) and decks (Ctrl+N/P), split and unsplit panels (\\ and |), move focus (Ctrl+F), collapse the node panel (Ctrl+S) and zoom a deck in place (Z). The p view picker, the Z zoom modal and the legacy panel modes are deleted, and glossary strands describe the new vocabulary.","design":"plan:202609/agents_tab_decks_and_cards.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
